A turn whose request a change closed, a bind or a wait's span, goes on without one while nobody waits,
so its own units give it time it runs as on spare time, and the next thread to wait takes the core from it whatever its deadline;
a turn its own units give time runs a request on them.

Caught-by: fuzz fuzz-pmp8 fuzz-rp2350 fuzz-work qemu-replay
Report: a turn its own units give time runs no request on them
Witness: fuzz bind-turn-later

diff --git a/kernel/sched.c b/kernel/sched.c
--- a/kernel/sched.c
+++ b/kernel/sched.c
@@ -1335,7 +1335,7 @@ void sched_tick(void)
 static __attribute__((noinline)) bool deadline_due(struct core *core)
 {
     struct place *p = turn_place(core), *own = turn_own(core);
-    if (p == NULL || own == NULL || place_units(p) == 0 || (core->run_queue == 0 && request_open(p, own))) {
+    if (p == NULL || own == NULL || place_units(p) == 0 || core->run_queue == 0) {
         return false;
     }
     uint64_t now = turn_close();
